{"title":"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Official_MAA)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Official MAA)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of positive integer divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/152ca730ea75dda1f1d50d7d9afb7ad02b87a3f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^9.$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> Three numbers are chosen independently and at random with replacement from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9fac87c49ed674bc76464b62e1faa1b0f2819f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> in the order they are chosen. The probability that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c80f7cbc6e8017ab735d473c6f3eb2e66a40511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269981c02d6475e9e4ac1869e1b063ef377c2847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b897aa5312f48ded1d6fa21afb4acfef70453ad3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(12cm); for (int x = 1; x &lt; 18; ++x) {     draw((x, 0) -- (x, 9), dotted); } for (int y = 1; y &lt; 9; ++y) {     draw((0, y) -- (18, y), dotted); }  draw((0, 0) -- (18, 0) -- (18, 9) -- (0, 9) -- cycle);  pair b1, b2, b3; pair c1, c2, c3; pair a1, a2, a3; b1 = (3, 0); b2 = (12, 0); b3 = (16, 0); c1 = (0, 2); c2 = (0, 4); c3 = (0, 8); a1 = b1 + c1; a2 = b2 + c2; a3 = b3 + c3;  draw(b1 -- a1 -- c1); draw(b2 -- a2 -- c2); draw(b3 -- a3 -- c3);  dot(a1); dot(a2); dot(a3); label(&quot;$a_1$&quot;, a1, NE); label(&quot;$a_2$&quot;, a2, NE); label(&quot;$a_3$&quot;, a3, NE); label(&quot;$b_1$&quot;, b1, S); label(&quot;$b_2$&quot;, b2, S); label(&quot;$b_3$&quot;, b3, S); label(&quot;$c_1$&quot;, c1, W); label(&quot;$c_2$&quot;, c2, W); label(&quot;$c_3$&quot;, c3, W);  [/asy]\" width=\"568\" height=\"298\" />\n</p><p>First, prime factorize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/2117d31bce44e57d672250338334262d0f660592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^9$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b5680cb6308dd6ec8e99c1239258108424844ad5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{18} \\cdot 5^9$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/51219511088b25365ab21b9c4304cf2392b1403e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{b_1} \\cdot 5^{c_1}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39511693919ec00000efde9bc9da693dbe8b0ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{b_2} \\cdot 5^{c_2}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd8f33445046ce95c03fd88a41f02e160cdadcad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{b_3} \\cdot 5^{c_3}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>In order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> to divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> to divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/028328419efa3d74ff700f0547591e9b521bfb00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1\\le b_2\\le b_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cfe6c8d69c969bdecab3956658f0221014b1728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1\\le c_2\\le c_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />. We will consider each case separately. Note that the total amount of possibilities is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e6380d8fc5c26c3c178eb1ab76a9b7f8570e0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$190^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />, as there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/5445971acf0556b280130fe5c654b789429a066c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(18+1)(9+1)=190$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" /> choices for each factor.\n</p><p>We notice that if we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b7aa611365e135f58aa09d52043ecd34855fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daf4b756601df3422c1b49b0012b42d82119cc0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, then we can reach the stronger inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c5d1ed269d5ee1ad85a061f7a26e1d70e29868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le b_1&lt;b_2+1&lt;b_3+2\\le 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"232\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, if we pick <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, they will correspond to a unique solution, forming a 1-1 correspondence between the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fc4b9ed6d75d026557e7b06c2ed483c6ed0eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16fd3a93fc80a2b65865bc2c7cdc456b54c26db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46dfc2bd76256db6fe92915a2b8b2ac01baa6427.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_3+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. This is also equivalent to applying stars and bars on distributing the powers of 2 and 5 through differences. The amount of solutions to this inequality is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31ebf8e658c95000bd6f8641c1e95e2d2a6f320f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{21}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>The case for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00322295674c54c5413520f7493470ff32ae3cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d4142d351ef99cc26a94e44c1912d904dd4a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94aaab012b431d7695fa1ae72d7a88b05baf09f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> proceeds similarly for a result of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29e639c0cda9832ae851d501c52d8383d8563782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{12}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\" />. Therefore, the probability of choosing three such factors is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/817cd42178e0b531ab9f976e36422ecf8aff72e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\dbinom{21}{3} \\cdot \\dbinom{12}{3}}{190^3}.\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"74\" /> Simplification gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9beb6abd3886b6b82158708551f0c1b34173b274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{77}{1805}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" />, and therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21751a7b8da5adcde99e006b96342618ee106db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{077}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-molocyxu\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Same as before, say the factors have powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f934684e96f0d1f5328705ee0de9c52ce7679ac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, b_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> can either be all distinct, all equal, or two of the three are equal. As well, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d71a3f5faf31e87ab07dfe44e27bc10c1e08b697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 \\leq b_2 \\leq b_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />. If they are all distinct, the number of cases is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25ab9e934cd7af58d709d2b6b9128edb3c592538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${19 \\choose 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\" />. If they are all equal, there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cases for the general value. If we have a pair equal, then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5df5f0494dd9461789f2e4e36c88a8f32fe6aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot {19\\choose 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"64\" height=\"53\" />. We need to multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because if we have two values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a0a6b9c28c969d8d6be9d0e51dff38a02c0e385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i &lt; b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />, we can have either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/e/e1e7b9d336e3617c37daa9e52b0502eb318d37b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_i, b_i, b_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/56428af821f7bbdfbd3efdc9a9026f30a75ac99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_i, b_j, b_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b6964a39cac249e2ec85607429575ab892582bac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{19 \\choose 3} + 2 \\cdot {19 \\choose 2} + 19 = 1330\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Likewise for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e42e04f664322ecd8bdbda8a537c417de766c199.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{10 \\choose 3} + 2 \\cdot {10 \\choose 2} + 10 = 220\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>The final probability is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e55e55922a88cb15ccf805c0de632b13378b2c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1330 \\cdot 220}{190^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />. Simplification gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9beb6abd3886b6b82158708551f0c1b34173b274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{77}{1805}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" />, and therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21751a7b8da5adcde99e006b96342618ee106db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{077}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to before, we calculate that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e6380d8fc5c26c3c178eb1ab76a9b7f8570e0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$190^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors with replacement. Then, we figure out the number of triplets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6465ec7d0ce2a741d0bbaa3a5998fd3bc338e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a,b,c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c1e03979c4740b28fb9b14e730c6610988e5887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${d,f,g}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> represent powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> represent powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, such that the triplets are in non-descending order. The maximum power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the maximum power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Using the Hockey Stick identity, we figure out that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29e639c0cda9832ae851d501c52d8383d8563782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{12}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31ebf8e658c95000bd6f8641c1e95e2d2a6f320f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{21}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Therefore, the probability of choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors which satisfy the conditions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/817cd42178e0b531ab9f976e36422ecf8aff72e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\dbinom{21}{3} \\cdot \\dbinom{12}{3}}{190^3}.\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"74\" /> This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9beb6abd3886b6b82158708551f0c1b34173b274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{77}{1805}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/628cf4cacc16de2b341c2ebd1abea7084569c8d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m =$\" width=\"34\" height=\"8\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21751a7b8da5adcde99e006b96342618ee106db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{077}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Official_MAA.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Official_MAA)\">Solution 4 (Official MAA)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Official MAA)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/2117d31bce44e57d672250338334262d0f660592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^9$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f63a2459f57428292f4cc0a300422f2b4340913d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{18}\\cdot5^{9}.$\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> The problem reduces to selecting independently the powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. This is equivalent to selecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> exponents for the powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> exponents for the powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and determining in each case the probability that the 3 exponents are chosen in nondecreasing order. Given a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the probability that three integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are chosen such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b3dc4e4132c56ac6252671835dfbfa23cc7115.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le a \\le b\\le c \\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" /> is the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/91927ed6d1093e6ce84e3aa8446121218cb17b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a606335fdc6ce417a886c086668f2b3182938b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> are chosen such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dc2636ee9abd09352bbc04c546582b8cd2b34d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le a &lt; b+1 &lt; c+2 \\le k+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"234\" height=\"15\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b0490434c2fd7ed2b3f839e588daaa576b5b999f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom {k+3}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"65\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/91927ed6d1093e6ce84e3aa8446121218cb17b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a606335fdc6ce417a886c086668f2b3182938b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />, so the probability that the integers are chosen in order is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/9391251b14c1426d1da570dc315d1e42c1177e79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\binom{k+3}3}{(k+1)^3}.\\]\" width=\"68\" height=\"46\" />Thus the probability that three chosen divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/2117d31bce44e57d672250338334262d0f660592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^9$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> satisfy the divisibility requirement is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/03955ece246623aee0a911000077b0bd6360ed6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\binom{12}3}{10^3}\\cdot\\frac{\\binom{21}3}{19^3}=\\frac{12\\cdot11\\cdot10}{6\\cdot10\\cdot10\\cdot10}\\cdot\\frac{21\\cdot20\\cdot19}{6\\cdot19\\cdot19\\cdot19}=\\frac{77}{1805}.\\]\" width=\"397\" height=\"42\" />The requested numerator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76e9de8e4daba1ef1f6eb3aa9d0d6be2e876a2bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of positive integer divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/152ca730ea75dda1f1d50d7d9afb7ad02b87a3f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^9.$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> Three numbers are chosen independently and at random with replacement from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9fac87c49ed674bc76464b62e1faa1b0f2819f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> in the order they are chosen. The probability that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c80f7cbc6e8017ab735d473c6f3eb2e66a40511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269981c02d6475e9e4ac1869e1b063ef377c2847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" />\n[rule]\nWe prime factorize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/2117d31bce44e57d672250338334262d0f660592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^9$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/7089e2c00e03f9911bc949ad16b293d7520e4887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{18}\\cdot 5^9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5da32b701e36840bbb889a4edc5de11f9e7510c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=2^x 5^y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f82b63a9b312ac363f65a3aa93a72c0c9ab0be9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 = 2^{x+a} 5^{y+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285ce063b601e0c07a3f81655b388301990f2329.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3 = a^{x+a+c} 5^{y+b+d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />. This choice of exponents guarantees that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62b9781a942fc743b2407e65b97af7b128e2306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+a+c&lt;18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4ab38a54bb1d4b663c598fb27e4f2c8b7a046a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+b+d&lt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34da901d31a766a26ce00bcc90d137649dcc8718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+a+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Then there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da2bde42728f00296108aca5a376b32761ab0c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{n+3-1}{3-1} = \\dbinom{n+2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"198\" height=\"55\" /> ways to pick <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be picked similarly. So, we would like to evaluate\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/2/f72f51b5b9262428e6e097c556afa8d20dcd411d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum\\limits_{n=0}^{18} \\dbinom{n+2}{2}\\right)\\left(\\sum\\limits_{m=0}^{9} \\dbinom{m+2}{2}\\right).\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"53\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fcc1321e45087aebb2bc7d28387330eee8703f4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{n+2}{2}=\\frac{(n+2)(n+1)}{2} = \\frac12 (n^2+3n+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"357\" height=\"55\" />, we get that the numerator is equal to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d314c9797b0d54dae36c415381e9d01dbebcc20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{(18)(19)(37)}{6} + \\frac{3(18)(19)}{2} + 38\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{(9)(10)(19)}{6} + \\frac{3(9)(10)}{2} + 18\\right) = 1330\\cdot220.\\]\" width=\"672\" height=\"43\" />\nThe denominator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e6380d8fc5c26c3c178eb1ab76a9b7f8570e0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$190^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />, so after simplifying we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9beb6abd3886b6b82158708551f0c1b34173b274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{77}{1805}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21751a7b8da5adcde99e006b96342618ee106db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{077}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Andrew2019\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I\" title=\"2020 AIME I\">2020 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?t